  "notes": ["The original archive is published once per two consecutive visual generations.","Each first visit binds the real model data. Thereafter the declared parent is inactive and moved, but its backing is retained.","With only one class-2 cell the original helper refuses another request in phases 2 and 3 before retirement, even after the selector-1 scene debit is returned.","Retirement detaches model pointers, returns the class-2 and descriptor cells, and frees the separate type-3 payload where present.","The next original constructor reuses the returned cell from a different declared parent with a new origin. The selector-1 lane flips from record 2 to 3.","The original archive owner and once-relocated bytes remain unchanged across both generations. This does not establish archive teardown.","Only bounded updates and draw-list preparation run. Video submission, live battle scheduling, and native gameplay are not qualified."],
